Usage: phpx {list|info|doctor|switch|ext|install|serve|run|remove|generate-config|sury|clean|self-update|known|variants|syntax|fpm|apache} <arguments>

Commands and Arguments:
  list
    Lists all installed PHP versions (CLI + FPM state), and shows the current default CLI.
  info <php_version>
    Shows a summarized phpinfo-style view for a specific version (binary, ini paths, key settings, extensions, FPM state).
    If no version is provided, uses the current default CLI version.
  doctor <php_version> [--fix]
    Runs sanity checks for a PHP version: CLI vs FPM mismatch, broken extensions, Apache module conflicts, FPM sizing hints.
    With --fix, it also:
      - cleans broken extension ini references (same as 'phpx clean <version>')
      - optionally disables extra Apache mod_php modules (keeps one).
  switch|s <php_version> [--no-web] [+ext] [-ext] [ext...]
    Switches to the specified PHP version (e.g., 8.2), installing it if not found.
    Also installs PHP-FPM if required for Nginx or Lighttpd, and configures the web server.
    Use --no-web to skip the web-server configuration wizard (useful in CI / CLI-only setups).
  ext|extensions|x [php_version] [--install="ext1,ext2"] [-y|--yes]
    Lists installed PHP extensions for the specified version and offers installation of new ones.
    If no version is provided, uses the currently active PHP version.
    - With --install, installs the given comma-separated list of extension names non-interactively.
    - Without --install, you will be prompted to choose extensions to install.
  known [--more]
    Lists PHP X.Y versions available from your current APT sources (useful after 'phpx sury').
    With --more, also prints the candidate package version for each X.Y.
  variants [--more]
    Shows local installed PHP versions and remote-available versions (APT) that are not installed locally.
    With --more, also prints the candidate package version for each remote X.Y.
  syntax [--exclude dir]... [--jobs N] [--php bin] [--no-progress] [extra_excludes...]
    Lints all *.php files under the current directory, printing only failures (single-line errors).
    Default excludes: vendor, node_modules. Progress is ON by default; disable with --no-progress.
  fpm {start|stop|restart|reload|status|enable|disable|test|config} [php_version]
    Controls the php-fpm service for a specific PHP version and can run config tests.
  apache {status|reload|restart|fpm|modphp} [php_version]
    Apache command suite; can wire Apache to PHP-FPM or mod_php for a specific PHP version.
  install|i composer
    Installs Composer globally if not already installed, then updates it.
  install|i <pecl_package(s)>
    Installs one or more PECL packages (comma-separated or space-separated). Example: xdebug,redis
  serve
    Starts a built-in PHP web server from the current or specified directory.
    Options include:
      --host <host>   (Default: 127.0.0.1)
      --port <port>   (Default: 8000)
      --root <dir>    (Default: current directory)
      --router <file> (Custom router script)
      -v|--verbose    (Verbose output)
  run <script_path> [php_version]
    Runs a PHP script using the specified or currently active PHP version.
  remove <php_version>
    Removes the specified PHP version and all related packages.
  remove <php_version> ext [--remove="ext1,ext2"]
    Removes selected PHP extensions for the given version.
    - With --remove, removes the given comma-separated list of extension names non-interactively.
    - Without --remove, you will be prompted to select extensions to remove.
  generate-config <environment> <php_version>
    Generates a PHP-FPM configuration and php.ini template for the given version and environment (production|development).
  sury
    Adds the Sury (or Ondrej) repository if needed (Debian/Ubuntu), enabling the latest PHP packages.
  clean
    Cleans up missing or broken extension references for a specified or current PHP version.
  self-update
    Updates the phpx script itself to the latest version from the official source.

Examples:
  phpx list
    Shows all installed PHP versions with CLI/FPM information.
  phpx info 8.3
    Displays a summarized config overview for PHP 8.3.
  phpx doctor 8.2 --fix
    Runs checks and cleans broken extensions / Apache PHP module conflicts for PHP 8.2.
  phpx switch 8.2 --no-web
    Switches to PHP 8.2 and sets it as CLI default, but skips web-server configuration.
  phpx ext 8.2 --install=redis,imagick
    Installs redis and imagick extensions for PHP 8.2 without interactive selection.
  phpx install composer
    Installs Composer globally if missing, then does a composer self-update.
  phpx install xdebug,redis
    Installs multiple PECL packages (e.g., xdebug and redis).
  phpx serve --host=192.168.0.1 --port=8080
    Serves the current directory on the specified host and port.
  phpx run my_script.php 8.2
    Runs 'my_script.php' with PHP version 8.2.
  phpx remove 8.1 ext --remove=redis,imagick
    Non-interactively removes redis and imagick extensions from PHP 8.1.
  phpx self-update
    Updates the phpx script to the latest version from GitHub.

Environment helpers:
  PHPX_LOG_DIR   Override log directory (for both root and non-root).
  PHPX_NO_LOG     If set, disables logging to file entirely.
  PHPX_ASSUME_YES If set, treats operations as if -y/--yes was passed (for non-interactive flows).

For more information or help, consult the script documentation or source code on GitHub.
